# Line endings here are part of behaviour, not taste.

# bash refuses a CRLF script, so the POSIX installer ships with LF whatever machine checked it out.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# cmd.exe parses labels and `goto` in a batch file differently depending on the build when the file is
# LF-only, and a raw-downloaded file is what the operator actually runs. So the bytes in the repository
# are the bytes that ship: `-text` turns off per-platform translation, and the files are committed with
# CRLF. `-text` also keeps the release workflow's byte-for-byte comparison of tag versus tree honest —
# an autocrlf checkout would differ from what raw.githubusercontent serves.
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text
